    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;11.06</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Histological differential diagnosis of conjunctival stromal tumour and ocular surface fibroma </span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Hardeep Singh Mudhar",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"943\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Histological features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Immunohistochemistry</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.3pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Molecular pathology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.45pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">References</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival stromal tumour</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Myxoid stroma; wiry to ropy collagen; bland spindle cells with pseudonuclear inclusions; multinucleated floret-like cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle cells: CD34+, PRKAR1A+, RB1+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Dendritic cells: factor&nbsp;XIIIa+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative for S100, SMA, desmin</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">None</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{22200094;26778331;31078543}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ocular surface fibroma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Collagenous stroma with mast cells; bland spindle cells; some occasional plumper spindle cells with very occasional pseudonuclear inclusions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle cells: CD34+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Dendritic cells: factor&nbsp;XIIIa+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative for S100, melan-A, SMA, desmin</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.3pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">None</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{6677850;3358733;17519675;32509765}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival myxoma (Carney complex)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Abundant myxoid stroma; mostly stellate cells; predominantly fibrillary collagen</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Stellate cells: CD34+, can be PRKAR1A&minus;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Some cases have factor&nbsp;XIIIa+ cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative for S100, SOX10, SMA</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mutations in <em>PRKAR1A</em> gene in 1&nbsp;case recorded</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{31078543}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Fat-free spindle cell lipoma and pleomorphic lipoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ropy collagen and myxoid stroma with mast cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle cell lipoma has short, stubby spindle cells with uniform elongated nuclei and bipolar eosinophilic cytoplasm; some cases show cytoplasmic vacuolation; spindle cells are usually arranged in short fascicles in a school-of-fish pattern, sometimes with nuclear palisading</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pleomorphic lipoma has pleomorphic spindle cells and multinucleated floret-like giant cells, which have peripheral radially placed hyperchromatic nuclei around central deeply eosinophilic cytoplasm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle cells: CD34+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">For other soft tissue sites: RB1 loss</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.3pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No available molecular data in conjunctiva</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">For other soft tissue sites: demonstration of loss of the <em>RB1</em> locus</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{24911538;30567236;22790852;12494468;21563233}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Neurofibroma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">May be solitary, diffuse, or plexiform; haphazard proliferation of spindle Schwann cells and fibroblasts, with mast cells present; degenerative atypia of cells can be seen; myxomatous stroma can be present; pseudomeissnerian corpuscles may be present; axons permeate the lesion</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle cells: patchy variable S100+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Axons: neurofilament+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No available molecular data in conjunctiva</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{2039037}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Solitary fibrous tumour</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Tapering spindle and ovoid/rounded cells; wiry interstitial collagen investing between individual spindle cells; multinucleated tumour giant cells can be present around pseudovascular spaces in giant cell&ndash;rich solitary fibrous tumour</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle and multinucleated cells: CD34+, STAT6+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Negative for SMA, S100, melan-A, desmin</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 106.3pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"142\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No available molecular data in conjunctiva</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.45pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{24216606;10366097;16219740;33123525;31698970}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 4cm; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Fibrous histiocytoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle to pleomorphic cells with conspicuous storiform to vaguely spindled architecture and a variably prominent collagenous or fibrous background</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 163pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"217\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spindle and pleomorphic cells: factor XIIIa+, CD68+, CD163+, &alpha;1-antitrypsin+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; 